00:07:44.686 --> 00:07:45.519
I'm satisfied.

00:07:45.519 --> 00:07:47.056
- Girl, your mouth to God's ear,

00:07:47.056 --> 00:07:49.830
but they're just so good and salty.

00:07:49.830 --> 00:07:52.150
No, but it, it was hard
to stop because I did,

00:07:52.150 --> 00:07:54.970
I was captivated by the story,
but I was also captivated

00:07:54.970 --> 00:07:58.590
by their love and support of
each other and it's a very

00:07:58.590 --> 00:08:01.030
intense, y'all play
very intense characters.

00:08:01.030 --> 00:08:01.863
- [Anne] Yeah.

00:08:01.863 --> 00:08:04.180
- And I just really appreciated
the relationship honestly.

00:08:04.180 --> 00:08:05.950
And I haven't watched
the entire thing yet.

00:08:05.950 --> 00:08:08.100
I'm almost done, but I,
'cause I had to sleep.

00:08:08.100 --> 00:08:09.890
I was like, I had like tape on my eyelids

00:08:09.890 --> 00:08:12.280
but I was, I was just, so engaged with it.

00:08:12.280 --> 00:08:14.120
And I thought this story was so well done.

00:08:14.120 --> 00:08:15.572
So why did you wanna do it?

00:08:15.572 --> 00:08:17.380
Why, what captivated you?

00:08:17.380 --> 00:08:20.740
- Well, it's this moment
that we're all living in

00:08:20.740 --> 00:08:22.500
and I don't know exactly what it is

00:08:22.500 --> 00:08:24.450
and it's a much larger conversation

00:08:24.450 --> 00:08:27.110
about what it is that
we're all going through

00:08:27.110 --> 00:08:29.030
that we really need
something to believe in.

00:08:29.030 --> 00:08:30.190
'Cause we all do, we all need

00:08:30.190 --> 00:08:32.640
we're all hoping that a unicorn is real.

00:08:32.640 --> 00:08:34.360
We're all hoping that, you know

00:08:34.360 --> 00:08:36.420
there's going to be kind
of a magic wand wave

00:08:36.420 --> 00:08:37.590
and we're gonna get a happy ending.

00:08:37.590 --> 00:08:41.340
And so we keep these stories
keep appealing to us.

00:08:41.340 --> 00:08:43.770
And I do believe that look

00:08:43.770 --> 00:08:45.230
there's a way to do this where

00:08:45.230 --> 00:08:47.867
like they're villains and
they're bad from the beginning.

00:08:47.867 --> 00:08:51.020
And I get that, but I also
think there's a version

00:08:51.020 --> 00:08:54.310
of it where that's probably a
little bit more true, which is

00:08:54.310 --> 00:08:57.600
that most people mean the
things that they say they intend

00:08:57.600 --> 00:08:58.620
for them to be true.

00:08:58.620 --> 00:09:00.690
Whether or not that person
is living the same reality

00:09:00.690 --> 00:09:02.750
as everyone else is up for debate.

00:09:02.750 --> 00:09:03.583
- Yeah.

00:09:03.583 --> 00:09:06.410
- And whether or not we would've noticed

00:09:06.410 --> 00:09:08.580
if that thing had eventually
come true that whole fake it

00:09:08.580 --> 00:09:09.413
until you make it thing.

00:09:09.413 --> 00:09:11.360
We notice when it doesn't come true.

00:09:11.360 --> 00:09:12.926
We notice when somebody didn't make it.

00:09:12.926 --> 00:09:13.774
- Yeah.

00:09:13.774 --> 00:09:16.080
- But we don't always notice when they do.

00:09:16.080 --> 00:09:19.430
So what is it about that
combination of us needing

00:09:19.430 --> 00:09:22.701
to believe in something and
be willing to go on that ride

00:09:22.701 --> 00:09:24.510
with the people who are willing to fake it

00:09:24.510 --> 00:09:25.343
till they make it.

00:09:25.343 --> 00:09:27.400
And how far are they willing to take it?

00:09:27.400 --> 00:09:29.642
I just wrote a song on Kelly Clarkson.

